35,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"Um... I found out that the suspended bay has a weight limit of four hundred kilos per square metre. Also, evening hires mean we have to be careful with displays that can't be closed or moved.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The data is quite telling. Visitors are drawn to movement and human presence; static, cased objects result in lower attendance and fewer repeat visits. We should prioritize an exhibition that is dynamic and interactive.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Rin,,"It's just as I feared! The conservation lab is almost empty, with only one person doing everything! And our volunteers are mostly just the town history group. We can't pick something that needs a ton of lab work!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"I knew it! Shipping is a mess. Two of our last four openings were delayed because of paperwork from distant lenders. Plus, transport and insurance are eating up a huge chunk of our installation budget!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It appears we are all uncovering rather sobering realities. I've discovered that bespoke mount-making is becoming prohibitively expensive, and our powered displays are prone to frequent, inconvenient breakdowns. We must be wary of high-maintenance machinery.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Benjamin, if powered displays break down often, maybe we should avoid anything too complex. And @Rin, if the lab is that short-staffed, we really can't afford a project with a lot of cleaning or stabilizing.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Daisuke, I agree. However, we must balance that with the fact that static displays fail to engage the public. We need a solution that provides activity without relying on fragile machinery or an absent staff.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Toshio, that's a tough puzzle! But if the lab is backed up with two hundred pieces, we definitely can't have an exhibition that adds more work for that one poor person. We need something simple to set up!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, if the mount-making costs are that high, we should look for things that come with their own supports. And we definitely need to avoid distant lenders if we don't want the opening to slip again!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, your point regarding the supports is most astute; it would be a tragedy to spend our budget on pedestals rather than art. We require a proposal that is fiscally prudent and mechanically modest.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I'm still worried about the weight limit and the evening hires. If we pick something with heavy objects or fragile, open setups, we might have another disaster with the floor or the caterers.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Daisuke, your concerns are valid. We must avoid heavy stonework or sprawling, fragile installations. The ideal choice will be lightweight, easy to secure for evening events, and yet offer the human interaction our visitors crave.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Rin,,"Wait, if the volunteers are mostly from the town history circle, maybe we can use that! We need an exhibition where people can actually talk and share stories, not just look at things in boxes.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, that's a great idea! If we use local people and things, we won't have to worry about those distant lenders and the shipping nightmares I found. Local is definitely the way to go!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, your enthusiasm for the local approach is quite infectious. It would certainly mitigate the risks of shipping delays and exorbitant transport costs, while perhaps sparing us from the joiner's rising rates.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think I agree. If we go with something local and lightweight, it should be safer for the floor and easier to manage around the evening bookings. It feels like the most responsible choice for the building.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"It seems we have found a common direction. A local, dynamic exhibition that utilizes human presence rather than complex machinery or heavy imports would satisfy both our operational constraints and our visitors' desires.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Rin,,I'm so glad we're on the same page! Let's make sure we pick something that lets our volunteers shine and doesn't make the lab person cry. I'm ready to see the candidates!,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"I'm ready too! Let's hope one of the options fits everything we've talked about. Local, simple, and exciting—that's the dream! Let's see what we've got to choose from!","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"Indeed, we have constructed a rather stringent set of criteria. I shall be looking for a candidate that is as fiscally discreet as it is operationally sustainable. Let us see if the proposals are as cooperative as we are.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
