60,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"Um... I think Option A is the safest. It's local, so it shouldn't be too heavy for the floor, and the demonstrations are easier to manage than big, open installations during evening hires.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"Option A aligns perfectly with the data. It provides the human presence and activity that visitors value, while avoiding the risks of heavy imports, fragile machinery, and an overburdened conservation lab.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Rin,,"I love Option A! It uses local craftspeople for demonstrations, which is way better than making the one lab person do everything. Plus, our town history volunteers will be perfect for this!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"Option A is definitely the winner! No distant lenders means no shipping delays or huge transport costs. It's local, simple, and it just fits everything we talked about. I'm voting for A!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Option A is a most elegant solution. It avoids the mechanical fragility of Option D, the logistical nightmares of Option B, and the lab's backlog in Option C. I vote for A.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,I... I agree. Option A seems to be the only one that doesn't risk damaging the floor or getting in the way of the evening hires. I'll vote for A as well.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"The consensus is absolute. Option A satisfies the visitor demand for interaction, respects our staffing shortages, and avoids the structural and financial pitfalls we identified. I also vote for A.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Rin,,"It's a total win-win! We get a great show, the volunteers get to help, and the lab person can finally catch up on their work. I'm voting for A too!","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Kenji,,I'm so happy we all agree! It's the perfect choice to keep things running smoothly and keep the visitors happy. A it is! I'm voting for A!,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"It is rare that a committee reaches such a harmonious conclusion so swiftly. Given that Option A is the only candidate that does not invite a financial or operational catastrophe, I concur. My vote is for A.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I... I think we've said everything. I'm happy we found a choice that doesn't put the building at risk. I'll cast my vote for A.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Toshio,,I concur. The evidence from the visitor records and our shared operational constraints makes Option A the only logical choice. I cast my vote for A.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Rin,,I'm so excited! This is going to be the best exhibition ever because everyone can help out. I'm voting for A!,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Kenji,,I'm all in! It's the safest and most exciting bet for everyone. I'm casting my vote for A!,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Since we have reached a state of total unanimity, I shall simply add my final confirmation. Logic and prudence both point toward the same conclusion. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
